        <mxCell id="ov-model-brief" parent="ov-layer" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=1;arcSize=5;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;spacing=18;" value="&lt;b&gt;Concurrency Model: Event-Driven + Thread Pool + Asynchronous Non-Blocking I/O&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Events—such as incoming connections, received data, timer expiry, and disconnections—trigger server processing.&lt;br&gt;The .NET thread pool executes ready continuations and game logic.&lt;br&gt;Pending network and database I/O does not occupy a waiting thread.&lt;br&gt;Each room processes actions sequentially, while different rooms run concurrently." vertex="1">
